Reference examples for graph `app`: one anchor, one edge, one action on that anchor, and a task that runs it.
Every template name stands for a real app's control.

### Anchor `app.feed`

`golden.md` -- what the screen is, fixed parts and changing parts:

```text
---
kind: page
---
Home feed: the tab bar along the bottom (feed, search, inbox, profile) with the feed tab
lit, the app's logo top left. The posts, their pictures and the unread counts change.
```

`main.ccat` -- only judges whether that screen is showing:

```ccat
// The logo is fixed and on this screen only. Search covers it, so an open search is not this screen.
if (has("feed_logo.png")) { return true }
return false
```

### Edge `app.entry-feed`

`main.ccat` -- only the move. The engine checks it starts on `entry` and gives `feed`
20 s to show up afterwards, so it never checks its own ends and never calls `goto`:

```ccat
// From the desktop into the app. A cold start puts the sign-in sheet up
// first; a warm start lands on the feed directly. Either way ends on the feed.
tap("app_icon.png")
wait(3000)                           // the captures put the app's first frame at ~1.5s; twice that
if (tap("sign_in.png")) {            // cold start only; on a warm start this is just false
  log("signed in on a cold start")
}
```

### Action `app.feed.claim`

`main.ccat` -- the claim. It starts and ends on `feed`; the engine checks both ends, runs it
once and does not retry, so spending or claiming goes here and not on an edge. The receipt
may cover the feed briefly. This script does not call `goto` or `at`. Its templates live in
this bundle.

```ccat
// Collects the daily reward, and says what it found.
defs {
  feed    = "feed.png"               // the feed tab, visible again once the receipt is gone
  claim   = "claim.png"              // the claim button, present only while the reward is unclaimed
  taken   = "claimed.png"            // the same button, greyed out once it is collected
  popup   = "reward_popup.png"       // the receipt sheet that shows only after a claim lands
  close_x = "popup_close.png"        // its top-right X
}

// "Already claimed" is a normal screen, not a failure, so it is a branch rather
// than a wait_until that would have to time out.
if (has(claim)) {
  tap(claim)
  wait_until(popup, 8000)            // the receipt shows only if the tap landed
  log("reward collected")
} elif (has(taken)) {
  log("already claimed today")
  return false                       // done, not failed -- the caller can tell the two apart
} else {
  log("neither the claim button nor its claimed state is on screen")
  return false                       // not the screen we expected; do not guess
}

// Close the receipt, bounded so a sheet that will not go away stops instead of
// spinning. Each close should land back on the feed.
loop(3) {
  if (has(popup)) {
    tap(close_x)
    wait_until(feed, 4000)
    log("closed the receipt")
  } else {
    break
  }
}

// The button is greyed only once the reward is ours. return true is what the
// engine then confirms is back on the feed; return false stops here.
if (wait_until(taken, 4000)) {
  log("daily claim done")            // grounded in the template just matched
  return true                        // confirmed: the reward is taken
} else {
  log("the claim never registered")
  return false
}
```

### Task `app.daily_claim`

`main.ccat` -- `goto` the page, `run` the action, then read its answer. The claim itself
stays in the action.

```ccat
// A task walks to the screen first. The graph checks both ends of every hop,
// so arriving is already confirmed; a screen it cannot reach is an error that
// names the hops, and the action does not run against the wrong screen.
goto("app:feed")

// Once. The action's log says whether it was already claimed or never landed.
// A false answer is this branch; a dead device or a stop is still an error.
if (run("app.feed.claim/main.ccat")) {
  log("daily claim done")
  return true
}
log("daily claim did not confirm")
return false
```
